title    Seven Eighths Fusion (2+2+1.5+1.5)
composer Claude
about    Revision of the 4-bar 7/8 fusion loop. Same harmony (Dm11, Bbmaj13#11, Gm9, altered A7) and tempo, re-phrased so the 3-eighth group splits into two equal 1.5-eighth pulses.

# Revision note. Listener feedback, verbatim: "fusion 7/8 wants 2 2 1.5 + 1.5
# like beat". Read as: the bar should be felt as four pulses, two of 2 eighths
# and two of 1.5 eighths (2+2+1.5+1.5 = 7). In sixteenth steps that is 4+4+3+3,
# so the pulses fall on steps 0, 4, 8 and 11.
#
# The original already put one kick on step 11, but every other part ignored
# it: the hats and the keys sat on step 12 (an even eighth grid), and the bass
# rolled root, b7, fifth on eighths. So the 3-group still felt like 3 eighths,
# with step 11 heard as a syncopation rather than a beat.
#
# What changed:
# - Drums: a four-pulse kick/snare cycle, kick on 0 and 8, backbeat snare on
#   4 and 11, so the two short pulses read as a compressed "1 2" after the
#   two long ones. Hat accents sit on all four pulses (0, 4, 8, 11), with the
#   in-between hats at 2, 6, 10, 13 (the midpoint of each 2-group, and the
#   last sixteenth of each 1.5-group).
# - Keys: the stab that was on step 12 moves to step 11, so the comping
#   rhythm is four strikes, one per pulse. In bar 4 the A7alt is struck on
#   8 and re-struck on 11 instead of held for 6 steps.
# - Bass: a note on every pulse start. The 3-group is now two 3-step notes
#   (root on 8, b7 or approach tone on 11) instead of root, b7, fifth.
# - Harmony, voicings, pad, tempo and the 7/8 meter are unchanged.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 120, so eighth beat = 240, with 14 sixteenth steps per bar.
tempo    240
beats    7
steps    2
swing    0

voice keys epiano vol=0.75 pan=-0.25
voice pad strings vol=0.35 pan=0.3
voice bass ebass vol=0.95
voice kick kick vol=0.95
voice snare snare vol=0.8
voice hat hat vol=0.55
voice crash crash vol=0.6

pattern A
# Keys: strikes on 0 (3 steps), 4 (2), 8 (2) and 11 (3), one per pulse.
# Voicings unchanged: Dm11 (F C E G A), Bbmaj13#11 (A D E G over Bb bass),
# Gm9 (Bb D F A over G bass), then A7alt (G C# F Bb C) on the two short
# pulses of bar 4.
keys | F3+C4+E4+G4+A4-- . F3+C4+E4+G4+A4- .- F3+C4+E4+G4+A4- . F3+C4+E4+G4+A4-- | A3+D4+E4+G4-- . A3+D4+E4+G4- .- A3+D4+E4+G4- . A3+D4+E4+G4-- | Bb3+D4+F4+A4-- . Bb3+D4+F4+A4- .- Bb3+D4+F4+A4- . Bb3+D4+F4+A4-- | Bb3+D4+F4+A4-- . Bb3+D4+F4+A4- .- G3+C#4+F4+Bb4+C5!-- G3+C#4+F4+Bb4+C5-- |
# Pad unchanged: common tones tied for three bars, F5+Bb5 on the A7alt.
pad  | E5+A5------------- | -------------- | -------------- | -------- F5+Bb5----- |
# Bass: a note on each pulse start (0, 4, 8, 11). Bar 4 lands A1 on step 8,
# then E2 on 11 and G2 leading back to D at the loop point.
bass | D2-- . A2-? .- D2-- C3-- | Bb1-- . F2-? .- Bb1-- A2-- | G1-- . D2-? .- G1-- F2-- | G1-- . D2-? .- A1!-- E2- G2 |
# Drums, grouped 4 4 3 3 to show the pulses.
kick  | x... .... x.. ... | % | % | x... .... x.. x.. |
snare | ..o. X... ... X.o | % | % | ..o. X... XoX XoX |
hat   | X.x. X.x. X.x X.x | % | % | X.x. X.x. X.. X.. |
crash | X... .... ... ... | _ | _ | _ |

loop A
